    "issued_at": "2026-09-25T05:49:00+00:00",
    "product_id": "797786ec-eaf9-4cd7-b335-a7bf352cb756",
    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 250549\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n1049 PM PDT Thu Sep 24 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n\n* Temperatures continue to warm through Saturday. \n\n\n* Increasing confidence in clouds, rainfall, and cooler readings \n  Sunday through Tuesday as tropical moisture spreads northward.\n\n&&\n\n\nA weak ridge will keep temperatures on the warm side with highs up \nto 5 degrees above average (mid 90s to low 100s in the desert \nvalleys) and lows around 5 to 10 degrees above average (the 70s). \nThis pattern breaks in the late weekend leading to cooler conditions \nand building cloud cover along with increasing humidity as a deep \ntrough approaches the area and pulls moisture from the south.\n\nModel agreement is really improving on the tough digging into the \nregion into the late weekend and centering over southern Nevada by \nMonday evening. This will lead to an initial moisture tap arriving \ninto the western protons of the CWA into Sunday, offering spotty \nstorm and shower activity focused over Arizona. As the trough \ncontinues to build through Sunday, tropical moisture from what will \nbe the remnants of Hurricane Polo begin to interact with that potion \nof the jet stream and pull northward. The main focus of the push of \nmoisture looks to be well to our east, however the low pressure \ncenter associated with the trough will wrap some of the moisture \ninto southern Nevada. This will lead to strong chances for showers \nand storms across the western half of the CWA, with the best chances \nalong focused over Mohave Co.  The sheer-rich environment along with \nthe cooler temperatures around the low pressure center could to \nbetter chances for severe storms Monday afternoon and into that \nnight. Rain chances look to exit Tuesday afternoon with quieter \nweather expected for the rest of the forecast period.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 06Z Forecast \nPackage...Southwesterly winds of less than 10 knots will continue \nthrough early Friday morning. Afterwards, easterly winds develop in \nthe late morning and early afternoon. Gusty southwesterly winds \nreturn in the late afternoon, decreasing after sunset. FEW to SCT \nmid and high clouds pass through the area throughout the forecast \nperiod. \n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 06Z Forecast Package...Winds will generally be \nlight through the night. A few showers remain in Lincoln County and \nover high terrain in Mohave County, but these are not expected to \nimpact any of the terminals. Dry conditions are expected tomorrow. \nGusty southwesterly winds pick up in the afternoon in the Las Vegas \nValley and gusty westerly winds develop at KDAG. Winds in the \nColorado River Valley mostly maintain a southerly direction. VFR \nconditions are expected. \n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Murdock\nAVIATION...Meltzer\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
